<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/warwick-shore.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/warwick-shore-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/warwick-shore.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/rhode-island-communities/">Communities</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span>Warwick</nav><p class="tag">Kent County &amp; West Bay</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Warwick, Rhode Island</h1><p class="lede">Warwick has dozens of miles of bay shoreline and the Pawtuxet River running through it. Coastal wind and river flooding both shape claims here.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn sun" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn glass" href="/request-a-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Kent County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Kent County &amp; West Bay</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="note"><p class="note-t">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips"><li>River flooding (flood policy)</li><li>Coastal wind</li><li>Tree fall</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Water damage</li></ul></div>
<p>Insurance appraisal in Warwick often starts with a question about water. The March 2010 flood showed how far the Pawtuxet River can rise, and homes along the bay remember the surge from past hurricanes. Flood damage falls under a flood policy, not a homeowner policy, so we spend time separating wind and rain damage, which a homeowner policy may cover, from rising water, which it generally excludes.</p>
<h2>Typical Warwick claims</h2>
<ul>
<li>Roof and siding damage on exposed shoreline neighborhoods during nor’easters</li>
<li>Trees down on houses and garages in older, wooded neighborhoods</li>
<li>Ice dams on capes with finished upper floors and little attic space</li>
<li>Basement and interior water damage from burst pipes or appliance leaks</li>
</ul>
<h2>Capes and ranches</h2>
<p>Postwar construction is simpler to scope than a Victorian, but estimates still miss items: knee-wall insulation behind ice-dam leaks, the full run of matching siding or the second layer of roofing that has to come off.</p><h2>Neighborhoods and villages we cover in Warwick</h2><ul class="chips plain"><li>Pawtuxet Village</li><li>Conimicut</li><li>Oakland Beach</li><li>Apponaug</li><li>Warwick Neck</li><li>Gaspee Plateau</li><li>Buttonwoods</li><li>Cowesett</li></ul><h2>Housing in Warwick</h2><p>Most of Warwick’s housing went up after World War II: capes, ranches and raised ranches on modest lots, with older cottages that became year-round homes near Oakland Beach, Conimicut and Buttonwoods, and larger waterfront houses on Warwick Neck.</p><h2>Warwick storm history</h2><ul class="mini-timeline"><li><b>1938 &amp; 1954</b><span>The 1938 hurricane and Hurricane Carol devastated the Oakland Beach shoreline.</span></li><li><b>2010</b><span>The Pawtuxet River reached record levels in March, flooding homes and businesses in Warwick and Cranston.</span></li><li><b>2012</b><span>Superstorm Sandy brought surge and wind damage to the Warwick shore.</span></li><li><b>2017</b><span>An October nor’easter downed trees and power lines across Kent County.</span></li></ul><h2>Services available in Warwick</h2><p>Every Rhode Island Insurance Appraiser service is available to owners in Warwick and nearby towns, including:</p><ul><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/appraisal-clause-advocacy/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/homeowner-claim-valuation/">Homeowner Claim Valuation</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/commercial-condo-hoa-claims/">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Claims</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/roof-hail-claim-valuation/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/wind-microburst-tornado-claims/">Wind, Microburst &amp; Tornado Damage</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/hurricane-tropical-storm-claims/">Hurricane &amp; Tropical Storm Claims</a></li><li><a href="/claim-valuation-services/water-leak-sewer-backup-claims/">Water Damage &amp; Leak Claims</a></li></ul><h2>Questions from Warwick owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Can appraisal resolve a flood claim?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Many flood policies, including those through the NFIP, have their own appraisal provisions with different rules. Your homeowner policy’s appraisal clause applies to covered homeowner losses, which generally exclude flood.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work near the airport and Apponaug?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Yes. We inspect throughout Warwick.</p></div></details><details><summary>My cape had an ice-dam leak. What gets missed?<svg class="ic chev" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"/></svg></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Wet insulation behind knee walls, ceiling and wall finishes to a logical break, and damaged roofing at the eaves are the usual gaps.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby communities</h2><div class="related"><a href="/rhode-island-communities/cranston/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Cranston</span><svg class="ic" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="fa